From 22430f182fcee27be045adbd54a2d7476b279caf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wisp <wisp@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:24:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] PS4 (Wisp): WebKit's pages in direct memory, not the flexible
 memory pool the app's processes share

OSAllocator commits (JSC's structure heap, conservative roots and the like) took flexible memory,
which comes out of one pool the app's processes share (about 450 MiB at the start, 1 GiB at most)
with every program image, thread stack and shared buffer; an empty pool freezes the app. They now
take pages of 2 MiB direct-memory blocks (the app has about 4.5 GiB), mapped where the commit is.
Decommit and releaseDecommitted (decommitAndRelease comes there with its memory still mapped) find
each page's place in direct memory with sceKernelVirtualQuery, unmap it, then give it back; a block
with nothing in use goes back to the kernel when two empty ones are kept. Flexible memory stays the
fallback when direct memory runs out, when the kernel does not say where a mapped page is (checked
once), and with WISP_WEBKIT_PAGES=flexible. The footprint WebKit's memory pressure handler reads
includes the pages in use.
---
 Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/MemoryPS4.cpp      |   7 +-
 Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/OSAllocatorPS4.cpp | 384 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 371 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

