diff --git a/Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/OSAllocatorPS4.cpp b/Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/OSAllocatorPS4.cpp
index d04e0b65..4e478389 100644
--- a/Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/OSAllocatorPS4.cpp
+++ b/Source/WTF/wtf/ps4/OSAllocatorPS4.cpp
@@ -12,9 +12,18 @@
  *
  *   reserve   sceKernelReserveVirtualRange with the alignment asked for, placed well above the
  *             kernel library's own allocations (as the kit's heap does)
- *   commit    flexible memory mapped MAP_FIXED over the range: the system pool first (as the kit's
- *             mmap does), then the app's regular pool
- *   decommit  a reservation mapped MAP_FIXED over the range again
+ *   commit    direct memory mapped MAP_FIXED over the range: pages of 2 MiB blocks this allocator
+ *             takes from the kernel; flexible memory (the system pool first, as the kit's mmap does,
+ *             then the app's regular pool) when there is no direct memory left
+ *   decommit  a reservation mapped MAP_FIXED over the range again; its direct memory goes back to
+ *             the blocks, and a block with nothing in use back to the kernel (two are kept)
+ *
+ * Why direct memory (Wisp v00.17; commits were flexible memory before): flexible memory comes out of
+ * one pool the app's processes share (about 450 MiB when the app starts, 1 GiB at most), which also
+ * holds every program image, thread stack and shared buffer, and an empty pool freezes the app (Wisp
+ * v00.13); the app has about 4.5 GiB of direct memory. WISP_WEBKIT_PAGES=flexible in the environment
+ * brings flexible memory back, and so does a kernel that does not say where a mapped page is in
+ * direct memory (checked once, before the first commit).
  *
  * The kernel's pages are 16 KiB; WTF's pageSize() may say 4 KiB (musl's getpagesize). Commits are
  * widened to whole kernel pages without remapping pages that already have memory, and decommits
@@ -29,10 +38,13 @@
